    {
      "name": "list_module_types",
      "description": "List the module types you can add, with their inputs, outputs and settings (name, min, max, default, unit). Pass a type to get just that one. Audio and control signals are voltages: pitch is 1 V per octave (0 V = C4), gates are 0/10 V. Drums can be synthesized with modules, the modular way (kick: a sine VCO whose pitch drops fast, through a VCA with a short envelope; snare: noise through a band-pass VCF with a brief envelope; hi-hat: noise high-passed, very short — see the \"Noise percussion\" preset), or played by samplers from the built-in kit (list_sounds, set_sample) for a quick result; both are triggered by a Trigger Seq. Choose from what the user asks for. Real instruments and voices (saxophone, vocals…) can’t be synthesized convincingly: use a sampler with a recording the user drops on it (or one of their saved sounds), or audioin (the user’s microphone or line input).",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "type": {
            "type": "string"
          }
